# =============================================================================
# Help24 backend — Docker build context exclusions
# =============================================================================
# Two jobs:
#   1. SPEED — everything listed here is never uploaded to the daemon, so the
#      context stays a few hundred KB instead of ~400 MB (node_modules alone).
#      A small context also means the `COPY` layers change less often, which is
#      what actually makes the build cache work.
#   2. SAFETY — `.env` must never enter a layer. Layers are permanent and
#      readable by anyone who can pull the image. Secrets are injected at RUN
#      time via compose `env_file:`, never at BUILD time.
#
# NOTE: *.spec.ts is deliberately NOT excluded — the Dockerfile has an optional
# `test` stage for CI. Spec files never reach the runtime image anyway, because
# tsconfig.build.json excludes them from `dist/` and the runner only copies
# `dist/`.
# =============================================================================

# ── Installed / generated artefacts ──────────────────────────────────────────
# node_modules is reinstalled inside the image from package-lock.json. Copying
# the host's copy would bake in Windows-native binaries that break on Linux.
node_modules
dist
*.tsbuildinfo
coverage

# ── Secrets — never bake these into an image ─────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
serviceAccount*.json
firebase-adminsdk*.json
google-services.json

# ── VCS, tooling, editors ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.git
.gitignore
.dockerignore
Dockerfile
docker-compose*.yml
.vscode
.idea
*.md

# ── Logs & OS noise ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
